{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"carnivoral-scarlet-chihuahua","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nBug `carbonous-bipartisan-ammonite` (46ec-e50d-49f6-4774, `b5d6e57cc01`) memoized the git toplevel per working directory in `_config_sources.repo_root`, and `rebar.show_ticket` now spawns 1 `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`. The CLI still spawns 4 for one `rebar show <id>`, because 3 other resolvers run their own uncached lookup.\n\nMeasured 2026-11-13 on origin/main `aa1681bb531` in a scratch repo with `REBAR_ROOT` unset (`GIT_TRACE2_EVENT`, plus a `subprocess.Popen` stack probe):\n1. `_config_sources.repo_root` (cached), from `_operation_config.compose_operation_snapshot` in `_cli/__init__._main_dispatch`.\n2. `_config_resolvers.repo_root_or_none` (`git -C . rev-parse --show-toplevel`, uncached), from `_cli/_init.ensure_store_mounted_best_effort`.\n3. `_config_resolvers.repo_root_or_none` again, from `_cli/_init.ensure_initialized` → `_resolve_repo_root`.\n4. `_engine_support/reads.tracker_dir` (`git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, uncached), from `reads_cli.main`.\nThe library path (`rebar.show_ticket`) makes 1.\n\n## Approach\nGive the 3 uncached sites the same per-(cwd, GIT_DIR, GIT_WORK_TREE) memo with the same stat-only revalidation that `repo_root` uses, so 1 process asks git once per working directory. Keep each caller's contract: `repo_root_or_none` still returns `None` outside a repository, still returns git's output verbatim and still discovers across filesystems; `reads.tracker_dir` still raises `TrackerRootError` outside a repository. `reset_config_cache` clears the shared memo. No new config key, env var or flag.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] An in-process `rebar show <id>` through the CLI entry point, with `REBAR_ROOT` unset, spawns at most 1 `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`; proved by a new test in `tests/unit/test_read_freshness_git_spawns.py`.\n- [ ] `repo_root_or_none` still returns `None` outside a repository, and a cwd change, a moved repository or a nested repository created later still resolve afresh.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/unit/test_read_freshness_git_spawns.py` passes.\n\n## Testing\nWrite the CLI spawn-count test first and watch it fail with 4, then fix. Add cases for the `None`-outside-a-repo and nested-repo contracts of `repo_root_or_none`. Run the file, `make verify`, and re-measure with `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT` in a scratch repo.","id":"7466-c6c6-f0ef-46c8","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"CLI reads still spawn several git toplevel lookups: rebar show makes 4"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794590366633642227,"uuid":"0b52194c-9ef0-4e79-a675-da8212e5e7f1"}